# README.md

After a change a **user or operator** would notice (CLI flags, HTTP/MCP, config files, protocol version, auth, connectors, harness commands, build tags), update [`README.md`](README.md) in the **same** change set.

Do:

- Quick start, env/`*Env`, Docker/compose, auth, MCP tools, protocol version, Go version if `go.mod` moved
- Link to [`planning/`](planning/) and [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md); do not duplicate the full spec
- Harness: `nerdctl compose`, `deploy/image/config`, goldens — only if those paths changed

Do not:

- Dump every internal refactor, test-only helper, or HMAC pepper name
- Invent APIs that are not in `planning/`

Example: new `sources[].type` → one README sentence + changelog entry; connection keys stay in `03`/`04`.
